            "source": [
                "# Q8:  In practice, adjusting the parameter β may be difficult, while one has often\n",
                "\n",
                "Avec cette nouvelle formulation, le problème d'optimisation équivaut à :  \n",
                "$$\n",
                "\\mathop{\\mathrm{arg\\,min}}_{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^N} ent(x) + \\iota_{[0, \\eta M \\sigma^2]}(||Kx - y||^2)\n",
                "$$\n",
                "\n",
                "$$\n",
                "\\iff\n",
                "$$\n",
                "\n",
                "$$\n",
                "\\mathop{\\mathrm{arg\\,min}}_{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^N} ent(x) + \\iota_{\\mathcal{B}(y, \\sqrt{\\eta M \\sigma^2})}(Kx)\n",
                "$$\n",
                "où  \n",
                "$\\tilde{\\mathcal{B}} := \\mathcal{B}\\left(y, \\sqrt{\\eta M\\sigma^2}\\right)$  \n",
                "est la boule centrée en $y$ et de rayon $\\sqrt{\\eta M\\sigma^2}$.  \n",
                "\n",
                "Nous sommes dans un cadre permettant d'utiliser l'algorithme d'optimisation Primal-Dual, qui résout  \n",
                "$$\n",
                "\\text{Argmin } f + h + g \\circ L\n",
                "$$  \n",
                "avec dans notre cas :  \n",
                "- $K \\in \\R^{N \\times M}$ comme opérateur linéaire $L$,  \n",
                "- $f := ent \\in \\Gamma_0(\\R^N)$,  \n",
                "- $g := \\iota_{\\tilde{\\mathcal{B}}} \\in \\Gamma_0(\\R^M)$,  \n",
                "- et $h = 0$ (ayant un gradient $\\beta$-Lipschitzien).  \n",
                "\n",
                "Nous avons déjà discuté de la manière de calculer $prox_{\\tau f}$.  \n",
                "En utilisant la formule de décomposition de Moreau, nous obtenons :  \n",
                "$$\n",
                "prox_{\\sigma g^*}(x) = x - \\sigma prox_{\\sigma^{-1}g}(\\sigma^{-1}x).\n",
                "$$  \n",
                "Dans ce cas, puisque $g = \\iota_{\\tilde{\\mathcal{B}}}$, son prox est facile à calculer, car il s'agit simplement de la projection $P_{\\tilde{\\mathcal{B}}}$, pour tout $\\sigma$.  \n",
                "\n",
                "Pour projeter un vecteur $x$ sur la boule centrée en $y$ de rayon $r$, on peut simplement appliquer :  \n",
                "- $x \\mapsto y + \\frac{r}{||x-y||}(x-y)$ (le mappage sur la sphère) si $x$ est en dehors de la boule,  \n",
                "- $x \\mapsto x$ si $x$ est à l'intérieur.",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["## Primal Dual Implementation"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 25,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "class g_indicator_ball(fun_minimize):\n",
                "    def __init__(self, y, radius, sigma):\n",
                "        self.y = y\n",
                "        self.radius = radius\n",
                "        self.sigma = sigma\n",
                "\n",
                '    def proximal(self, x: "np.array") -> "np.array":\n',
                '        """Projection onto the ball"""\n',
                "        diff = x - self.y\n",
                "        norm_diff = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n",
                "\n",
                "        if norm_diff <= self.radius:\n",
                "            return x\n",
                "        else:\n",
                "            return self.y + (self.radius / norm_diff) * diff\n",
                "        \n",
                '    def proximal_conjugate(self, v: "np.array") -> "np.array":\n',
                '        """Moreau decomposition formula"""\n',
                "        return v - self.sigma*self.proximal(v/self.sigma)\n",
                "        \n",
                "    def __call__(self, x):\n",
                "        if np.linalg.norm(x - self.y) <= self.radius:\n",
                "            return 0\n",
                "        else:\n",
                "            return np.inf",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 26,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "def primal_dual(x0,v0,tau,sigma,y,K,radius,num_iter,verbose=True):\n",
                "    x_n=x0\n",
                "    v_n=v0\n",
                "    f=g_entropy(gamma=tau)\n",
                "    g=g_indicator_ball(y, radius, sigma=sigma)\n",
                "    square_norm=f_square_norm(K,y)\n",
                "    loss=[]\n",
                "    for n in range(num_iter):\n",
                "        x_n_1=f.proximal(x_n - tau*K.T @ v_n)\n",
                "        v_n=g.proximal_conjugate(v_n + sigma*K@(2*x_n_1 - x_n))\n",
                "        x_n=x_n_1\n",
                "        if n%10000==0 and verbose:\n",
                '            print("iteration",n,"the loss is",f(x_n)+square_norm(x_n))\n',
                "        loss.append(f(x_n)+square_norm(x_n))\n",
                "\n",
                '        #print("iteration",n,"the loss is",f(x_n)+g(x_n))#"loss f",f(x_n),"loss g",g(x_n))\n',
                "    return x_n,loss",
            ],
